    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d298">

                <pb facs="0295" n="283" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg283"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">870.811/231: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Rumania</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gunther</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bucharest</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-02-11T21:00:00+02:00">February 11,
                            1941—9 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 12—2:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>135. My 812 of December 13, 6 p.m.<anchor n="30" xml:id="d298-f1"/> The recent
                    anarchistic riots in Rumania prevented the reopening of the Danubian Conference
                    on January 21 as had been planned. The Director of the Political Section <pb
                        facs="0296" n="284" xml:id="pg284"/> of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs told
                        Huston<anchor n="31" xml:id="d298-f2"/> yesterday that it was hoped that the
                    various delegations could reassemble in the near future, perhaps towards the end
                    of February or sometime in March. He stated that in as much as the Russian
                    demands had heretofore been so far removed from acceptability by the other
                    delegates as to preclude the reaching of any agreement, the Rumanians were now
                    engaged in the elaboration of a compromise proposal which they hoped could form
                    the basis of fresh discussions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gunther</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
